      "body": "## Summary\n\nPrepare core 0.59.0 and chart 0.46.0 from c22ead2802effe5562e7723a9320ad08a0df7fea (#779), matching the 19-file scope of b8cc4ce2 (#777). Includes the four exact Changelog lines since v0.58.0 (three Added, one Fixed), the chart entry dated 2026-10-26, versioned install docs and code-checked operator upgrade notes.\n\nBump the shared version and all 21 internal exact pins; keep the tui wildcard. Both main locks change only the 24 workspace version lines; each fixture lock changes only three path-crate version lines. The branch retains stock Wasmtime. No WIT or SDK contract change, provider re-pin, release tag or publication.\n\n## Security impact\n\nRelease prep only: versions, changelog, upgrade notes, locks and rebuilt fixtures; no code change.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Head SHA | `875d21abc28bb759438a7899eded644f4c9fc218` |\n| Toolchain | Rust 1.98.1; wasm-tools 1.259.0; cargo-deny 0.20.2; inherited CARGO_HOME and default target directories |\n| `git diff --check` | Passed, including the committed diff against the base |\n| `cargo fmt --all --check` | Passed |\n| `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` | Passed |\n| `ci/fetch-external-provider-components.sh examples/providers` | Passed; curl-only, attestations variable unset; all three external artifacts verified |\n| `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked --lib --bins --tests` with RUST_LOG unset | Passed: 3,342 tests across 79 executables; 0 failed, 0 ignored; no reruns or root-only failures (UID 1000) |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --workspace --all-features --no-deps` | Passed |\n| `python3 .github/scripts/check_docs_duplicates.py docs README.md AGENTS.md crates/*/README.md` | Passed, 49 Markdown files |\n| `.github/scripts/verify-release-metadata.py --metadata <(cargo metadata --locked --no-deps --format-version 1) --plan .github/release-crates.txt --changelog CHANGELOG.md` | Passed; 0.59.0 changelog and 21 publishable crates validated |\n| `.github/scripts/verify_changelog.py --changelog CHANGELOG.md --entry dekopon-chart-0.46.0` | Passed |\n| `cargo deny --all-features check` | Passed: advisories, bans, licenses and sources |\n| `cargo package --workspace --locked --no-verify` | Passed, all 24 workspace crates |\n| Optimized lock pinned-source `cargo tree --locked -p \"$spec\"` with the optimization config | Passed in the isolated worktree after lock regeneration; Wasmtime 49.0.4 at `6e850d9e9df96b0eacd6867e8ffb8a813200e42f` |\n| Five fixture updates, pinned build scripts and clean rebuild comparisons | Passed; removed each fixture's target between builds and verified identical SHA-256 hashes below |\n| Additional checks: exact file-set comparison with #777 and version-only comparison of all seven locks | Passed: exactly 19 files; no extra lock changes |\n| `cargo test --doc`, `cargo machete`, `cargo check --release` | Not run locally; left to CI by the brief |\n| Broader CI matrix: daemon dependency gates, SDK Wasm check, shellcheck, provider-workspace tests, ARM64 host tests, audit-event docs gate, chart checks, CLI install, memory lab and optimized build/tests | Not run locally; outside the requested local CI subset |\n\nEach component reproduced byte for byte:\n\n| Fixture | SHA-256 | Clean rebuild |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cli-probe | `f95bfeeabe2429669ca8eed264660833af9c54c6482aed35cdae14bbe23133c7` | Identical |\n| clock-probe | `5cd2c9ada43e4a3e6dbdadc6ef3b0121a636a3dedea7a574e32bed442ab23da3` | Identical |\n| http-probe | `a9dffeadd77cfa33791b7b435d092786b385095371a3089fe2847d6919ad4615` | Identical |\n| storage-probe | `bd1a91edf5dfc1db713b0d5b8713443c1ab97cb646a3c4b09b648a313c6d60ff` | Identical |\n| memory-smoke-probe | `eb721817f4207e29a64a68165d720979a101a413311aabdb14477799f27984d4` | Identical |\n\n## Limitations / follow-ups\n\nRemote CI and the coordinator-launched Astra review and Claude review remain pending. No self-review was run or cited. This checkpoint does not merge, tag or publish the release.\n\n## Choices I made\n\n1. Read `revert-safe` as configuration and journal compatibility: 0.58.0 can read journals written by 0.59.0 without migration, since these changes alter neither their format nor their keys. Downgrading removes the new memory notice, exit-status telemetry and ordinary-HTTP redirect redaction; it does not retain 0.59.0 behavior. The notice adds prompt text and a telemetry record, not a stored journal record.\n2. Restored the two temporary worktree files (`Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock`) after the pinned-source check, then ran the specified worktree removal; this allowed removal of the otherwise dirty isolated checkout without discarding branch changes.\n",
